{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794358586279,"sessionID":"ses_e37e4f349ffe51J6s9LdQyAxPv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01a1c81b289e719d8a2cb412","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # App\n2: \n3: ## Run contract\n4: \n5: - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n6: - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n7: - The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n8: - Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n9: \n10: ## Layout\n11: \n12: - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n13: - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n14: \n15: Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n\n(End of file - total 15 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/README.md","text":"# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":15,"totalLines":15,"truncated":false}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1794358586235,"end":1794358586273}},"id":"prt_1c81b2b6f001aSXx6QA9BonZUG","sessionID":"ses_e37e4f349ffe51J6s9LdQyAxPv","messageID":"msg_1c81b1366001EoVCj875Sd6PaX"}}
