{"type":"text","timestamp":1794359209359,"sessionID":"ses_e37e4f349ffe51J6s9LdQyAxPv","part":{"id":"prt_1c824ad7e001aFrnX7CRb9bZvx","messageID":"msg_1c82494b7001RCEHBqb0E5uHoY","sessionID":"ses_e37e4f349ffe51J6s9LdQyAxPv","type":"text","text":"<think>Playwright is installable via npx. Do we have browsers installed? `ls /root/.cache/ms-playwright` returned nothing (permission denied maybe). Let me try installing chromium to test the frontend E2E. It might be a large download but the sandbox has network access to npm. Let me check if browsers can be downloaded (playwright downloads from CDN — the sandbox may not have access to that CDN; it said \"The sandbox can install packages from the public package registries (through a read-only cache); it has no other network access.\" So the Playwright browser CDN is likely blocked.\n\nLet me try `npx playwright install chromium` and see. If it fails, I'll test the frontend differently (e.g., with a JSDOM-based test, or by careful review).\n\nActually, let me check whether a chromium/chrome binary exists in the environment.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794359209342,"end":1794359209356}}}
